          "content": "Here's what I found:\n\n**Why FreeCAD WebGL export is slow for lofts/curved surfaces:**\n\n1. **Single-core limitation**: FreeCAD can only utilize a single CPU core for most operations, which significantly impacts performance on complex geometry.\n\n2. **Tessellation overhead**: Curved surfaces like lofts require tessellation (converting smooth surfaces into triangular meshes) for WebGL export. This process is computationally intensive, especially for complex B-spline surfaces.\n\n3. **Memory usage**: Loft operations can consume excessive RAM and cause performance degradation, particularly with complex multi-section lofts.\n\n**Ways to speed up WebGL export:**\n\n1. **Adjust tessellation settings**: \n   - Go to **Edit > Preferences > Part Design > Shape View**\n   - Increase tessellation value from default 0.5% to 1.0% or higher (coarser mesh = faster)\n   - Content was rephrased for compliance with licensing restrictions\n\n2. **Use Mesh Workbench for better control**:\n   - Switch to **Mesh Design Workbench**\n   - Use **\"Tessellate shape\"** tool with custom parameters\n   - Export the optimized mesh instead of the original solid\n   - Content was rephrased for compliance with licensing restrictions\n\n3. **Simplify geometry before export**:\n   - Reduce the number of loft sections if possible\n   - Use simpler airfoil profiles\n   - Consider using fewer control points in B-splines\n\n4. **Export native FreeCAD models**: WebGL export works better with native FreeCAD geometry versus imported models (STEP, etc.).\n\n**For your blade loft specifically**: Consider reducing the tessellation quality for WebGL export while keeping high quality for the actual CAD model.\n\nReferences:\n[1] Performance optimization - https://forum.freecad.org/viewtopic.php?t=95669\n[2] Is there a setting for export resolution? - https://forum.freecad.org/viewtopic.php?t=13658\n[3] Freecad 1.0 freezing on export of fillets - https://forum.freecad.org/viewtopic.php?start=20&t=94237\n[4] Bad performance and freezing - https://forum.freecad.org/viewtopic.php?start=10&t=45561"
