    "> tell me more about bsplines",
    "## B-Splines Fundamentals\n\n### What B-splines Are:\n**B-splines** (Basis splines) are mathematical curves defined by:\n- **Control points** - points that influence the curve shape but the curve doesn't necessarily pass through them\n- **Knot vector** - parameter values that determine where the curve segments join\n- **Degree** - determines smoothness (degree 1 = linear, degree 3 = cubic)\n\n### Key Differences:\n\n**Interpolation vs Approximation:**\n- **Interpolation**: Curve passes **exactly** through all data points\n- **Approximation**: Curve is **influenced** by data points but may not pass through them\n\n**Control Points vs Data Points:**\n- **Data points**: What you want the curve to represent\n- **Control points**: Mathematical points that define the curve (often different locations)\n\n### FreeCAD B-spline Methods:\n\n```python\n# Method 1: Interpolation (passes through points)\ncurve = Part.BSplineCurve()\ncurve.interpolate(data_points)  # Curve goes through each point\n\n# Method 2: Approximation (influenced by points)  \ncurve = Part.BSplineCurve()\ncurve.approximate(data_points)  # Curve approximates the shape\n\n# Method 3: Direct control points\ncurve = Part.BSplineCurve()\ncurve.buildFromPoles(control_points)  # Direct control over curve\n```\n\n### For Your Morphing System:\n- **Interpolation** gives exact control over key points\n- **Control point manipulation** allows smooth deformation\n- **Knot insertion** lets you add constraints at specific locations\n\nWhich aspect interests you most?\n[Tool uses: none]",
