    "Here's what I found about approaches for moving clusters of control points in interpolated B-splines:\n\n## Key Approaches for Control Point Cluster Manipulation:\n\n### 1. **Free-Form Deformation (FFD)**\nFrom [AIAA research](https://arc.aiaa.org/doi/10.2514/6.2023-3601), FFD creates a deformation box around geometry and moves the B-spline control point net as a group. This allows **cluster-based manipulation** while maintaining curve smoothness.\n\n### 2. **Local Modification Principle**\n[Michigan Tech documentation](https://pages.mtu.edu/~shene/COURSES/cs3621/NOTES/spline/B-spline/bspline-mv-ctlpt.html) explains that moving control point Pi only affects the curve on interval [ui, ui+p+1]. This means **adjacent control points can be moved together** without affecting distant parts of the curve.\n\n### 3. **Geometry-Aware Control Point Deformation**\n[ArXiv research](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2201.01873) describes neural network approaches for **intuitive piecewise smooth deformations** that work well for manufactured objects like airfoils.\n\n### 4. **Cluster Deformation Techniques**\n- **Proportional scaling**: Move control points with weights based on distance from target\n- **Constraint-based**: Maintain specific geometric relationships between control points\n- **Smooth transitions**: Use falloff functions to blend deformation across cluster boundaries\n\n## For Your Airfoil Morphing:\n\n**Recommended approach**: Use **weighted cluster deformation** where:\n- Each cluster moves toward its target shape (triangle vertices)\n- **Smooth falloff** between clusters maintains curve continuity\n- **Preserve local curve properties** while achieving global shape change\n\nContent was rephrased for compliance with licensing restrictions.\n\nReferences:\n[1] Free-Form Deformation of Parametric CAD Geometry via B-Spline Transformations - https://arc.aiaa.org/doi/10.2514/6.2023-3601\n[2] Moving Control Points - https://pages.mtu.edu/~shene/COURSES/cs3621/NOTES/spline/B-spline/bspline-mv-ctlpt.html\n[3] Geometry-Aware Control Point Deformation - https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2201.01873\n[Tool uses: none]",
