- (-50, 300, 15))\n        = (-43.75, 300, 10.75)  # Halfway between airfoil and triangle\n```\n\nThis gives **smooth, predictable morphing** where each control point moves in a **straight line** from its Station 5 position to its target triangle position.\n[Tool uses: none]",
    "> what does calculate_target_point look like?",
    "Here's what `calculate_target_point()` would look like:\n\n```python\ndef calculate_target_point(cp_index, y_position, cluster_type):\n    \"\"\"Calculate target triangle position for a control point\"\"\"\n    \n    # Triangle geometry at this y position\n    trailing_x = -wood_width + (wood_width - W) * (y_position / blade_radius)  # X stretch\n    leading_x = 50  # Always at section boundary\n    bottom_z = 0    # Triangle base\n    top_z = thickness - (thickness - thicknesses[section_index]) * (y_position / blade_radius)  # Section height\n    min_thickness = 0.5  # Minimal trailing edge thickness\n    \n    if cluster_type == 'bottom':\n        # Bottom cluster: line from trailing to leading along base\n        progress = cp_index / 39  # 0 to 1 across bottom cluster\n        target_x = trailing_x + progress * (leading_x - trailing_x)\n        target_z = bottom_z + progress * (top_z - bottom_z)  # 0 to section height\n        \n    elif cluster_type == 'leading':\n        # Leading point: always at corner\n        target_x = leading_x  # 50\n        target_z = top_z      # Section height (13 at root)\n        \n    elif cluster_type == 'top':\n        # Top cluster: line from leading back to trailing (with minimal thickness)\n        progress = (cp_index - 41) / 39  # 0 to 1 across top cluster\n        target_x = leading_x + progress * (trailing_x - leading_x)\n        target_z = top_z + progress * (min_thickness - top_z)  # Section height to minimal\n    \n    return FreeCAD.Vector(target_x, y_position, target_z)\n```\n\n## Key Points:\n\n1. **Uses actual section geometry** - trailing_x, leading_x calculated from blade parameters\n2. **Handles X-axis stretch** - trailing edge moves from -100 to -125 as y decreases  \n3. **Maintains triangle shape** - bottom and top clusters form triangle edges\n4. **Preserves minimal thickness** - top cluster ends at 0.5mm above bottom\n5. **Parametric along clusters** - progress (0-1) distributes points evenly along triangle edges\n\nThis ensures each control point has a **specific, geometrically correct target** in the triangle shape at any y position.\n[Tool uses: none]",
